// UNSOUNDNESS repro (reviewer finding A2): a `since` whose LEFT operand
// reads `u`, where `u` is restricted only by a LATER conjunct. The since's
// anchor (`Login{}`) restricts nothing about `u`, so evaluation checks the
// left per step with `u` unbound — independent re-quantification per step.
// The same formula changes verdict under `&&`-commutation: on {Transfer
// carol, Login, Read bob, Read alice} this order evaluates TRUE while the
// restrictor-first order (and MFOTL) gives FALSE. The safety condition requires
// free(left) ⊆ free(right) for β S γ; Dogwood relaxes that to "or restricted
// by a PRECEDING conjunct" — this policy satisfies neither.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    exists (u: String). (
        (Drupe::Action::"Read"::request{ input.user: u } since within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{})
        && formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: u }
    )
};
